1
00:01:59,719 --> 00:02:00,000
At ease!

2
00:02:01,239 --> 00:02:01,560
Attention!

3
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,079
Right, dress!

4
00:02:04,879 --> 00:02:05,439
Eyes front!

5
00:02:06,519 --> 00:02:08,879
Five kilometers plus 100 log squats.

6
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:10,520
Towards Heijiao Rock.

7
00:02:18,039 --> 00:02:18,840
You don't have to join us.

8
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,479
Five kilometers? I ran that every day at the police academy.

9
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:28,599
Left, face!

10
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,080
Double time, march!

11
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,800
One! One, two, one!

12
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,919
One, two, one!

13
00:02:49,199 --> 00:02:50,400
Train your body!

14
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:53,199
Train your body, stay ready!

15
00:02:53,199 --> 00:02:55,960
Build your muscle, take a beating!

16
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,560
Not bad at all.

17
00:03:13,319 --> 00:03:14,719
Two point five kilometers.

18
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:18,960
We're halfway through our Long March!

19
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:22,120
That was just the warm-up.

20
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:25,000
We sprint the second half. Pick up the pace!

21
00:03:26,719 --> 00:03:27,400
A sprint?

22
00:03:30,039 --> 00:03:32,599
Train your body, stay ready!

23
00:03:35,439 --> 00:03:37,599
Lao Na, I'm on my morning run. What's up?

24
00:03:38,479 --> 00:03:39,560
Didn't you text me...

25
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,639
...asking me to call you?

26
00:03:41,759 --> 00:03:42,800
Must be pretty urgent then.

27
00:03:42,919 --> 00:03:43,680
Who's in a rush?

28
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:45,800
Does it have to be right now?

29
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,319
Alright, alright.

30
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,599
See you at the Municipal Bureau.

31
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,080
Okay, okay.

32
00:03:52,319 --> 00:03:53,439
That Lao Na from CID...

33
00:03:53,439 --> 00:03:54,199
Get back to work.

34
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,479
Train your body, stay ready!

35
00:03:59,159 --> 00:04:00,000
Train your body...

36
00:04:01,439 --> 00:04:02,240
...take a beating!

37
00:04:08,919 --> 00:04:10,719
That call from Lao Na came at the perfect time.

38
00:04:13,759 --> 00:04:15,719
We've checked all the cameras around the mahjong parlor.

39
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,240
Didn't find anyone suspicious.

40
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,800
Shows they have strong counter-surveillance skills.

41
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,399
They're deliberately avoiding the cameras.

42
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:24,000
What about immigration? We've been there.

43
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,360
Let's screen the foreigners in Hongye first.

44
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,360
See if we get any results.

45
00:04:30,279 --> 00:04:30,959
Commissar Tan.

46
00:04:31,959 --> 00:04:32,959
SWAT team isn't busy?

47
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,519
I'm very busy.

48
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,279
Just finished my morning workout.

49
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:37,120
Let me tell you.

50
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,120
I could easily beat you in a 3K run right now.

51
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,360
Your gut doesn't look any smaller.

52
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:43,480
You...

53
00:04:43,959 --> 00:04:44,920
You're hiding from something, aren't you?

54
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,240
What would I be hiding from?

55
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:46,839
I need to talk to you about something.

56
00:04:46,839 --> 00:04:47,639
What for?

57
00:04:49,519 --> 00:04:50,759
It's Jin Yonggang's father.

58
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,040
He wants to claim his son's body.

59
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,160
Unbelievable, you two are really something.

60
00:04:55,319 --> 00:04:55,560
You...

61
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,560
Ji Min called me yesterday and I told her.

62
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:58,519
He can't claim it for now.

63
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:01,079
What do you mean by "for now"?

64
00:05:01,079 --> 00:05:03,279
Give me a timeframe for "for now."

65
00:05:03,639 --> 00:05:06,160
"For now" means not right now, got it?

66
00:05:09,959 --> 00:05:10,720
Why are you asking him?

67
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:11,759
He's... He's in charge of this.

68
00:05:13,279 --> 00:05:13,680
Come on.

69
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,040
Read between the lines.

70
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:20,040
Wasn't Jin Yonggang shot dead?

71
00:05:22,279 --> 00:05:23,199
The case isn't closed yet.

72
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,240
Keep it confidential.

73
00:05:27,959 --> 00:05:29,279
Inside information, not to be leaked.

74
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,480
Hear me?

75
00:05:32,439 --> 00:05:34,600
Especially from the SWAT team.

76
00:05:34,839 --> 00:05:35,639
Confidential, got it.

77
00:05:37,319 --> 00:05:38,959
If the body can't be claimed for now...

78
00:05:38,959 --> 00:05:39,199
Then...

79
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:42,519
Can the old man at least see his son?

80
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:48,040
I've got things to do. You two chat.

81
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:49,519
You...

82
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,360
Hey! Hey what?

83
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,279
I'm talking to you.

84
00:05:51,279 --> 00:05:52,160
Why are you calling him?

85
00:05:52,439 --> 00:05:53,160
He's not in charge of this anyway.

86
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,240
Talk to Chief Guo.

87
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:57,079
Come on, are you kidding me?

88
00:05:57,079 --> 00:05:58,759
You want me to go to Chief Guo for this little thing?

89
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,079
Go to Chief Guo, go to Chief Guo.

90
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:07,279
Xiao Tan.

91
00:06:07,839 --> 00:06:09,600
Good thing I ran into you today.

92
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,399
Look at my memory.

93
00:06:12,439 --> 00:06:14,480
I couldn't remember where I lived for a second.

94
00:06:14,959 --> 00:06:15,519
Mr. Jin.

95
00:06:15,759 --> 00:06:17,000
You can't leave your keys here.

96
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:19,040
Keep your keys safe.

97
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:19,600
Okay, okay.

98
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:20,839
Come, take a seat.

99
00:06:20,839 --> 00:06:21,240
I shouldn't stay.

100
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,199
Let me leave you my phone number.

101
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,480
Look, Xiao Min's number is right here.

102
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,040
If you need anything...

103
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,920
Just call Xiao Min...

104
00:06:28,439 --> 00:06:29,879
Or... call me.

105
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:36,759
17653774686.

106
00:06:36,759 --> 00:06:37,199
Okay.

107
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:38,639
Xiao Tan.

108
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,439
You and Xiao Min need to be good to each other.

109
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:42,279
Treat each other well, you two.

110
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,680
We will, we will. Don't worry.

111
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:44,480
Good.

112
00:06:44,519 --> 00:06:45,000
I'll get going.

113
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:45,399
You...

114
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:46,560
I won't keep you then.

115
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,720
Get some good rest. Rest well.

116
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:48,519
Okay.

117
00:06:48,519 --> 00:06:49,279
Call me if you need anything!

118
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,079
Alright. You sure you won't stay?

119
00:06:51,079 --> 00:06:51,560
No, I should go.

120
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,560
You two treat each other well!

121
00:06:52,639 --> 00:06:53,079
Alright.

122
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:53,839
Good, good.

123
00:07:12,279 --> 00:07:12,839
Time for meds.

124
00:07:19,519 --> 00:07:20,680
Two red ones.

125
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:22,800
One white one.

126
00:07:44,279 --> 00:07:46,120
Today I'll teach you how to make meat buns.

127
00:07:46,279 --> 00:07:47,040
First, let's

128
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,800
go over the ingredients we prepared today.

129
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,439
First is the ground pork belly filling,

130
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,439
flour, green beans, radishes,

131
00:07:52,759 --> 00:07:53,480
scallion-ginger water,

132
00:07:54,079 --> 00:07:54,800
thirteen-spice powder,

133
00:07:55,439 --> 00:07:55,959
chopped scallions,

134
00:07:56,199 --> 00:07:57,920
sugar, salt, and chicken bouillon.

135
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,279
You're back.

136
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:06,720
I came up with a new filling today.

137
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:07,839
What kind of filling?

138
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:08,759
Smell it. Smell it.

139
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:09,839
It smells amazing.

140
00:08:11,519 --> 00:08:12,480
It really does smell good.

141
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,480
Take a break.

142
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,439
You can have a few more later.

143
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,919
I ran into Mr. Jin at the Bureau today.

144
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,480
I guess his old condition acted up again.

145
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
He couldn't find his way home.

146
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,279
Good thing he ran into me.

147
00:08:49,519 --> 00:08:50,559
He couldn't find his way home?

148
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,120
With something this serious,

149
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,519
why didn't you call me?

150
00:08:58,759 --> 00:09:00,039
Seeing how you've been lately,

151
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,159
so incredibly anxious,

152
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,480
and I happened to be free,

153
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,919
I just took him straight home.

154
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:07,519
He...

155
00:09:08,039 --> 00:09:09,120
How was he doing?

156
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:10,679
He seemed fine.

157
00:09:13,159 --> 00:09:13,799
And then?

158
00:09:14,279 --> 00:09:15,879
And then I took him home.

159
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:18,039
Walked him all the way inside.

160
00:09:18,639 --> 00:09:20,960
And then I came back to work on the new filling.

161
00:09:24,759 --> 00:09:25,480
Don't overthink it.

162
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:29,120
Mr. Jin was in much better spirits at home.

163
00:09:31,559 --> 00:09:33,399
He even thanked me before I left.

164
00:09:35,519 --> 00:09:37,840
He also told you to take care of yourself,

165
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:40,000
and not work so hard all the time.

166
00:09:42,759 --> 00:09:44,600
And told us to be good to each other.

167
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,240
What did you say?

168
00:09:50,879 --> 00:09:53,799
I said Mr. Jin told us to be good to each other.

169
00:10:07,679 --> 00:10:08,399
Who are you calling?

170
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,080
Are you heading out?

171
00:10:19,919 --> 00:10:20,799
You're not eating the buns?

172
00:11:03,639 --> 00:11:04,399
Mr. Jin!

173
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:10,600
No one's here.

174
00:11:11,919 --> 00:11:12,720
Mr. Jin!

175
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:21,039
Mr. Jin!

176
00:11:23,039 --> 00:11:23,679
Mr. Jin!

177
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,399
Preliminary ruling is suicide.

178
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:46,720
I'm leaving.

179
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:04,200
Get in the car.

180
00:13:09,639 --> 00:13:10,679
Min, it's going to rain.

181
00:13:10,679 --> 00:13:11,679
Let's go home.

182
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,519
I know you're hurting.

183
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,240
I took Mr. Jin home at noon.

184
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,440
He was perfectly fine.

185
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,080
I never expected him to be gone by tonight.

186
00:13:39,879 --> 00:13:40,559
Tan Yan.

187
00:13:42,879 --> 00:13:44,879
Have you ever truly listened to me?

188
00:13:45,399 --> 00:13:46,879
I always listen to you.

189
00:13:46,879 --> 00:13:48,200
Then haven't I told you...

190
00:13:48,399 --> 00:13:50,559
...that Mr. Jin was like a father to me?

191
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:52,320
When you saw Mr. Jin today...

192
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:54,039
...why didn't you call me?

193
00:14:04,279 --> 00:14:05,519
Didn't I do all this

194
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,120
for your sake?

195
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,840
I did it because I was thinking of you!

196
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,559
Thinking of me?

197
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,399
Back when I was in CID,

198
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,320
you made me go back to Hongye.

199
00:14:20,559 --> 00:14:22,159
Now that I'm doing just fine at the local station,

200
00:14:22,679 --> 00:14:24,360
you insist on transferring me to the archives.

201
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:25,720
Is that really for my sake?

202
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,399
It's my fault.

203
00:14:43,159 --> 00:14:44,200
I took matters into my own hands.

204
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:47,799
Let's go home.

205
00:14:54,759 --> 00:14:56,559
I haven't finished making the buns for you yet.

206
00:14:59,559 --> 00:15:00,679
Were you really making them for me?

207
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:01,720
Of course.

208
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:04,919
And taking some to Lao Guo while I'm at it.

209
00:15:06,879 --> 00:15:07,919
I'm the afterthought, aren't I?

210
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:10,919
I'm an afterthought in your plans.

211
00:15:10,919 --> 00:15:12,159
An afterthought in your care.

212
00:15:12,159 --> 00:15:13,080
An afterthought when you humor me.

213
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,240
An afterthought in your affection.

214
00:15:14,679 --> 00:15:15,799
Have you ever asked me

215
00:15:15,799 --> 00:15:17,039
if I actually need any of it?

216
00:15:17,039 --> 00:15:18,080
What I actually need?

217
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,080
Or if I even want it?

218
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:37,639
It wasn't like this before.

219
00:15:41,399 --> 00:15:43,000
As a couple, I'm a part of you

220
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:43,919
and you're a part of me.

221
00:15:44,279 --> 00:15:45,399
Do you even have to ask?

222
00:15:55,639 --> 00:15:56,120
Let's go home.

223
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,000
Where did the old Tan Yan go?

224
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:03,679
I'm here.

225
00:16:04,279 --> 00:16:04,720
I'm here.

226
00:16:05,159 --> 00:16:05,840
I'm right here.

227
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:07,519
I'm here.

228
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:12,559
Don't be mad.

229
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:20,759
It's thundering.

230
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:21,840
It's raining.

231
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:23,159
You won't look pretty if you get wet.

232
00:16:23,279 --> 00:16:24,000
Let's separate.

233
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:31,759
Morning, Commissar. Morning.

234
00:19:32,359 --> 00:19:32,680
Morning.

235
00:19:34,759 --> 00:19:36,039
Could've at least helped me.

236
00:19:36,039 --> 00:19:36,519
Unbelievable.

237
00:19:45,599 --> 00:19:46,279
Morning, Captain Liao.

238
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:48,920
Morning, Commissar Tan.

239
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:52,000
From now on, just be on time for morning drills.

240
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,119
No need to come so early.

241
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:54,359
I've decided.

242
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:57,000
Starting today, I'm planting roots in the SWAT detachment.

243
00:19:59,000 --> 00:19:59,519
You

244
00:19:59,759 --> 00:20:00,759
have a family.

245
00:20:01,599 --> 00:20:03,200
Just keep your phone on 24/7.

246
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,319
And commute normally.

247
00:20:04,759 --> 00:20:06,000
If I don't immerse myself in the team,

248
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:07,480
how can I be a good commissar?

249
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:09,519
And I'd fail our leaders' expectations.

250
00:20:11,839 --> 00:20:12,519
Captain Liao, Captain Liao.

251
00:20:14,519 --> 00:20:15,519
I've thought about it carefully.

252
00:20:16,839 --> 00:20:17,440
Before,

253
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:21,000
there was a disconnect between me and the guys.

254
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:23,720
I want to spend day and night with them.

255
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:24,839
Stand together with them.

256
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:26,039
And resolve it little by little.

257
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:27,599
You'd better be sure, Commissar Tan.

258
00:20:28,599 --> 00:20:31,039
The dorms here can't compare to home.

259
00:20:31,559 --> 00:20:32,640
There are no single rooms.

260
00:20:33,359 --> 00:20:34,319
Or private bathrooms.

261
00:20:35,279 --> 00:20:36,160
I'm afraid you won't get used to it.

262
00:20:37,359 --> 00:20:39,079
To integrate into a new team,

263
00:20:39,079 --> 00:20:40,720
sacrificing a bit of personal life

264
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,240
is nothing.

265
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:45,440
Chief Ji doesn't mind?

266
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,200
We're both police officers.

267
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,680
What's not to understand?

268
00:20:50,039 --> 00:20:50,960
Let's see where I'll be staying.

269
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:51,920
Arrange a spot for me.

270
00:20:52,599 --> 00:20:53,079
Lu Xiao!

271
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:56,079
Yes, sir!

272
00:20:58,680 --> 00:21:00,920
Quickly take Commissar Tan's luggage to my room.

273
00:21:04,799 --> 00:21:05,839
Commissar Tan is staying in the dorms?

274
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,079
I'm sharing a room with you?

275
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:19,440
Made it, made it.

276
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,480
How's the leg? Any reaction?

277
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:23,559
It hurts.

278
00:21:23,799 --> 00:21:24,440
That's normal.

279
00:21:24,599 --> 00:21:25,359
Normal, normal.

280
00:21:30,559 --> 00:21:31,200
Attention!

281
00:21:33,319 --> 00:21:33,759
At ease!

282
00:21:36,839 --> 00:21:38,240
Starting today,

283
